<board>
<plain>
<wire x1="0" y1="0" x2="60.96" y2="0" width="0" layer="20"/>
<wire x1="60.96" y1="0" x2="60.96" y2="25.4" width="0" layer="20"/>
<wire x1="60.96" y1="25.4" x2="0" y2="25.4" width="0" layer="20"/>
<wire x1="0" y1="25.4" x2="0" y2="0" width="0" layer="20"/>
<text x="0" y="57.75" size="0.7" layer="51" ratio="12">Footprint provenance -- moved off the board, originals live in the ctambe library</text>
<text x="0" y="56.65" size="0.6" layer="51" ratio="10">X3 -- DM3AT-SF-PEJM5</text>
<text x="2" y="55.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">Hirose DM3AT-SF-PEJM5. Contacts: 8 at P=1.1, pad 0.70x1.20,</text>
<text x="2" y="55" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">span 7.70 -- EXACT per datasheet p3 (pitch confirmed against the</text>
<text x="2" y="54.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">PDF vector geometry). Shield pads G1-G4 derived from the drawing's</text>
<text x="2" y="53.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">dimension chains: VERIFY against the Hirose PCB pattern.</text>
<text x="2" y="52.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">Layer 39 box is the card + 21.55 mm eject stroke: keep clear.</text>
<text x="2" y="52" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">Card-detect switch terminals have no land -- design uses DAT3 CD.</text>
<text x="0" y="50.65" size="0.6" layer="51" ratio="10">U8 -- LTC3569-QFN20</text>
<text x="2" y="49.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">LTC3569EUDC UDC 3x4 QFN-20. Land per datasheet p23: 0.50 BSC,</text>
<text x="2" y="49" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">pad 0.70x0.25, outer 3.50/4.50, exposed pad 1.65x2.65. EXACT.</text>
<text x="0" y="47.65" size="0.6" layer="51" ratio="10">X1 -- MOLEX-105017-0001</text>
<text x="2" y="46.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">Molex 105017-0001 micro-USB-B, bottom mount, B type, flangeless.</text>
<text x="2" y="46" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">Rebuilt from SD-105017-001 sheet 1, RECOMMENDED P.C.B. PATTERN</text>
<text x="2" y="45.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">LAYOUT, measured off the drawing's vector geometry. Scale set by</text>
<text x="2" y="44.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">the 5.00 between hole centres, checked against the 1.45 land</text>
<text x="2" y="43.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">(1.4467 measured) and the 0.85 drill (0.8426). Origin is the rear</text>
<text x="2" y="43" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">row centreline; +y is the PCB EDGE and the mouth.</text>
<text x="2" y="42.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">LAYER 48 carries the PCB EDGE line at y +4.141. It must fall on</text>
<text x="2" y="41.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">the board outline -- check_board.py enforces it. The mating face</text>
<text x="2" y="40.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">is 0.70 further out at +4.841, so the shell OVERHANGS the edge.</text>
<text x="2" y="40" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">MS1/MS2 are PLATED SLOTS, 0.60 x 1.30 at x +/-3.50, drawn on LAYER</text>
<text x="2" y="39.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">46 as ZERO-WIDTH outlines, which is what JLCPCB's own Eagle article</text>
<text x="2" y="38.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">asks for. Their CAM job merges layer 46 into the GKO outline, so</text>
<text x="2" y="37.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">the slot reaches them -- but a slot in the outline layer does not</text>
<text x="2" y="37" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">say whether it is plated. ADD AN ORDER NOTE naming these two as</text>
<text x="2" y="36.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">PLATED. The 0.60 pad drill inside each slot is intentional: drill</text>
<text x="2" y="35.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">first, then rout. STILL UNCONFIRMED: a plated slot sitting INSIDE</text>
<text x="2" y="34.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">an SMD land. Nothing JLCPCB publishes covers it -- ask them.</text>
<text x="2" y="34" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">PIN 1 IS AT +X. Corrected 2026-08-28. The drawing's RECOMMENDED P.C.B.</text>
<text x="2" y="33.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">PATTERN is a TOP view with the connector front at -y and PIN 1 at -x. This</text>
<text x="2" y="32.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">footprint puts the front at +y, which is a 180 degree rotation of that view,</text>
<text x="2" y="31.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">so PIN 1 has to move to +x as well. It was built by flipping y only, which</text>
<text x="2" y="31" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">MIRRORS the pin order: VBUS landed on the shell's GND contact and GND on</text>
<text x="2" y="30.25" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">VBUS -- a dead short across the cable on plug-in -- while D- drove the ID</text>
<text x="2" y="29.5" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">contact and the real D- contact sat on X1.4, which is not connected. Only D+</text>
<text x="2" y="28.75" size="0.5" layer="51" ratio="10">was right, because it is the centre pad and survives the mirror.</text>
</plain>
