<designrules name="Zulu A7 6 layer JLCPCB">
<description language="en">&lt;b&gt;Zulu A7 &amp;mdash; 6 layer, JLCPCB&lt;/b&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;This is the active fab.&lt;/b&gt; The escape closes here, and the number that makes it close is not a fab capability at all &amp;mdash; it is the &lt;b&gt;ball land, taken from 0.275 to 0.225&amp;nbsp;mm&lt;/b&gt;. UG475 gives 0.275 as a MAXIMUM, and the gap between two lands is 0.5&amp;nbsp;&amp;minus;&amp;nbsp;land, so the land is the one term in w&amp;nbsp;+&amp;nbsp;2s that is ours to choose. At 0.225 the gap is 0.275&amp;nbsp;mm, and a 3&amp;nbsp;mil trace at 3.5&amp;nbsp;mil clearance needs 0.2562. It clears by &lt;b&gt;0.0188&amp;nbsp;mm&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;p&gt;That is why msWidth is 0.0762&amp;nbsp;mm (3&amp;nbsp;mil) while every clearance is 0.09&amp;nbsp;mm (JLCPCB's published 3.5&amp;nbsp;mil). &lt;b&gt;CONFIRMED BY JLCPCB 2026-08-27.&lt;/b&gt; They pointed at the capability table row &lt;i&gt;Min. track width and spacing (1 oz)&lt;/i&gt;, which reads &quot;Multilayer: 0.09 / 0.09&amp;nbsp;mm (3.5 / 3.5&amp;nbsp;mil). 3&amp;nbsp;mil is acceptable in BGA fan-outs&quot;. Two things follow, and together they mean &lt;b&gt;this board needs nothing agreed&lt;/b&gt;. First, the 0.09&amp;nbsp;mm clearance used everywhere here IS the published multilayer minimum, so the spacing is not a concession at all &amp;mdash; only the 0.0762&amp;nbsp;mm WIDTH is below standard, and the same sentence grants it. Even on the narrowest possible reading of &quot;3&amp;nbsp;mil&quot; &amp;mdash; width only &amp;mdash; the design is inside their table as printed. Second, that row is the &lt;b&gt;1&amp;nbsp;oz&lt;/b&gt; row, so the allowance holds at standard copper weight and needs no lighter foil (the 2&amp;nbsp;oz row drops to 0.15/0.15 multilayer, so the weight does matter). PCBWay by contrast puts its 3.5/3.5 only on the 18&amp;nbsp;um row.&lt;p&gt;Whether &quot;3&amp;nbsp;mil&quot; ALSO covers spacing is still unstated, and it is now only an optional upgrade: at 3/3 the land could rise to 0.250 (0.91:1 rather than 0.82:1). It is not free &amp;mdash; a 0.250 land leaves a 0.250&amp;nbsp;mm gap, which the present 0.0762/0.0900 does NOT fit (0.2562), so it would force 3&amp;nbsp;mil spacing through the whole fan-out and re-cut the escape geometry. Staying at 0.225 is the recommendation. Either way it costs &lt;b&gt;+20&amp;nbsp;% of the order&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; JLCPCB's surcharge for 3.0&amp;ndash;3.5&amp;nbsp;mil on a 4&amp;ndash;8 layer board.&lt;p&gt;3&amp;nbsp;mil is a DRC floor used in one place, the ring&amp;nbsp;1 row crossing. Everything outside the ball field is drawn at 0.09&amp;nbsp;mm or wider.&lt;p&gt;Vias are 0.2&amp;nbsp;mm drill with a 0.05&amp;nbsp;mm ring, so a 0.30&amp;nbsp;mm land &amp;mdash; JLCPCB's published minimum is 0.15/0.25&amp;nbsp;mm, but 0.15 through 1.6&amp;nbsp;mm is 10.7:1 and over the 10:1 ceiling, where 0.2&amp;nbsp;mm is 8.0:1. No blind vias, no buried vias, no microvias: JLCPCB makes through holes only, which is also why msMicroVia is parked at 9.9&amp;nbsp;mm.&lt;p&gt;Solder mask opening is NOT set in the footprint. It falls out of mlMinStopFrame = 0.05&amp;nbsp;mm, so the 0.225 land gets a 0.325&amp;nbsp;mm opening, leaving a 0.175&amp;nbsp;mm (6.9&amp;nbsp;mil) dam between adjacent openings with the escape trace running under it. Confirm JLCPCB will hold that.&lt;p&gt;Stackup is JLC06161H-3313, their only 6-layer 1.6&amp;nbsp;mm build: 3313 prepreg 0.0994 under L1 and over L6, 2116 prepreg 0.1164 between L3 and L4, 0.55&amp;nbsp;mm cores at L2/L3 and L4/L5. Outer copper 35&amp;nbsp;um, inner 15.2&amp;nbsp;um &amp;mdash; inner is 0.5&amp;nbsp;oz by default here, unlike PCBWay. Trace widths in board/STACKUP.md follow from these.&lt;p&gt;NOT a fab confirmation. Every figure above is from JLCPCB's published capability tables plus this package's geometry (tools/escape/options.py). Check it against their current sheet before ordering.</description>
